# =============================================================================
# Flash TETHER — environment template (Nile testnet / course project)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Next.js loads .env.local automatically. Do not commit .env.local.
# Never paste private keys into git, chat, or screenshots.
#
# Required for mint:     TRON_PRIVATE_KEY, FLASH_CONTRACT_ADDRESS
# Strongly recommended:  TRONGRID_API_KEY
# Optional / leftover:   RECEIVER_ADDRESS, NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRON_PRIVATE_KEY  (required)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 64-character hex private key of the CONTRACT OWNER wallet. No 0x prefix.
# The server uses this only in src/lib/tron.ts to sign flashMint().
# It MUST be the same account that deployed contracts/FlashTETHER.sol
# (flashMint is onlyOwner).
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Install TronLink: https://www.tronlink.org
#   2. Create or import a wallet and switch the network to Nile Testnet
#      (TronLink → network selector → Nile).
#   3. Fund it with test TRX: https://nileex.io/join/getJoinPage
#   4. Export the key: TronLink → Account / Security → Export Private Key
#      (password required). Paste the 64 hex characters below.
#
# You can also generate a throwaway Nile key with TronWeb for local classwork:
#   node -e "const {TronWeb}=require('tronweb'); const a=TronWeb.createRandom();
#            console.log(a.privateKey); console.log(a.address);"
#
# If this key ever leaked, move ownership or redeploy — do not keep using it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRON_PRIVATE_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRONGRID_API_KEY  (strongly recommended)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sent as the TRON-PRO-API-KEY header on TronGrid RPC calls.
# Without it, public TronGrid rate limits will fail mints under load.
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Open https://www.trongrid.io/dashboard
#   2. Sign in with GitHub or email
#   3. Create a project → Create API Key
#   4. Copy the UUID (example shape: 11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555)
#
# Nile and mainnet keys are created in the same dashboard. Use the key with
# the Nile host (https://nile.trongrid.io) for this course project.
# Docs: https://developers.tron.network/reference/select-network
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TRONGRID_API_KEY=


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FLASH_CONTRACT_ADDRESS  (required)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base58 Tron address of the deployed demo contract (starts with T, 34 chars).
# Returned to the UI after a successful mint and used as the TronWeb target.
#
# How to get it:
#   1. Get Nile test TRX in the owner wallet (same as TRON_PRIVATE_KEY)
#   2. Open Nile TronIDE: https://nileide.tronscan.org
#   3. New file → paste contracts/FlashTETHER.sol
#   4. Compile with Solidity 0.8.x
#   5. Connect TronLink on Nile → Deploy
#   6. Copy the deployed contract address from the success panel
#      or from https://nile.tronscan.org/#/address/<your-owner-address>
#
# Confirm it looks like: T + 33 more Base58 characters (no 0, O, I, l).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FLASH_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TRON_NETWORK  (optional — unused by current source)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Informal label only. src/ does not read this variable today.
# If you add network switching later, use "nile" for this course project.
#
# Allowed values if you start using it:  nile
# Do not set mainnet for this assignment.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRON_NETWORK=nile
